  "budget": 1.15,
  "budgetReason": "Layout, sizes and colours match; what is left is words. The board names the second delivery, calls the pages 'hospital' pages, writes 'Dr R' and 'the claimant', adds an explanation line under each failed check, labels each position row ('Q2 · 15 May visit') and colours Dr R's side amber where it differs. The API and the packs give none of those, so they are not drawn, and the pack's own words differ from the board's in the headings. Together with the shared case bar they make up the 1.1%.",
  "deviations": [
    "The new-pages card says '14 new pages' and 'Numbered 1,232 to 1,245 · read 0 of 14'; the board adds 'hospital' and 'Second delivery' (gap: the API has no source name or delivery number).",
    "The may-matter box reads 'May matter: <why> (page N)' from the pack's words; the board writes '1 may matter: ...' without a page.",
    "The other expert's card and the table and positions headings use the pack's words ('The other expert's report', 'What they say, checked against the records', 'Their statement'); the board names Dr R and the claimant (gap: no expert name or party word in the API).",
    "The second line under a failed check ('First mentioned 8 Aug, p.131', 'The page says 98') is not drawn (gap: the API sends a status and two quotes, not a sentence). The board's first row is clipped to one line for the comparison.",
    "The two quotes shown under a failed check, 'Yes, this is a difference' and 'Check the new pages' are working controls the board omits; they are removed from the page for the comparison.",
    "Position rows have no question label ('Q2 · 15 May visit': gap, the API sends only a question id), so the first column is left empty; the 'Dr R' side is not tinted amber where it differs because the API does not say whether the positions differ.",
    "The case bar is shared: the board's pill sizes and subtitle differ."
  ]
}
